## Security and privacy

Transaction processing happens in the browser. Imported source files are not uploaded, and ledger contents are excluded from story saves. CSV parsing validates headers and row structure and limits each import to 10,000 transactions. CSV exports escape cells and guard against common spreadsheet formula-injection prefixes.

Story saves use browser-local storage and are not encrypted. The local preview server binds to the loopback interface. There are no account credentials or external AI service secrets to configure.

## Efficiency and accessibility

Canvas rendering uses cached terrain, and the application has no runtime package dependencies or remote media requests. Keyboard controls cover movement, interactions, and dialogue choices; touch controls and mouse-selectable dialogue choices are also available. Audio is optional and starts only after user activation.

The canvas-based world has limited screen-reader accessibility. This version does not claim full accessibility compliance.

## Testing

The existing verification records **26 passing automated tests**, covering movement, collision, dash behavior, hidden passage gating, story choices, both endings, saved state, corrupt-save recovery, CSV validation, and exports. Run `npm test` to reproduce the automated checks.

Recorded browser testing completed both endings through game controls, checked save/reload and JSON checkpoint restoration, and reviewed a real three-row CSV with downloaded reviewed and excluded outputs. The standalone build was tested through local HTTP; direct `file://` execution was not verified by browser automation.

## Assumptions and scope

- Transaction imports need distinct date, description/merchant, and amount columns. Currency is optional and defaults to USD when absent.
- Reliable recurring-payment analysis needs supported year-first dates. Category suggestions and recurring hints are heuristics, not financial advice or guaranteed classifications.
- Progress is local to the current browser and origin unless exported. There is no cloud synchronization.
- The adventure is a small, complete vertical slice. Combat, mining, crafting, procedural worlds, and multiplayer are outside its scope.
